Description: Provide cross-compiling default for libc access method (OHOS/musl)

Upstream configure.in uses AC_TRY_RUN to detect how to obtain a handle
to libc at runtime (dlsym((void*)-1) vs dlopen("libc...")). When
cross-compiling (OHOS aarch64 target) the run tests cannot execute; the
underscore probe already defaults to "no" (correct for musl), but
without a libc-access method configure aborts with:

    configure: error: cannot figure out how to access libc

This patch gives the "can we access libc without dlopen" probe a
cross-compiling action that assumes musl semantics, where
dlopen("libc.so", RTLD_LAZY) returns the already-loaded libc handle
(musl's dlopen special-cases libc.so). Only the cross path changes;
native builds are unaffected.

--- a/configure.in
+++ b/configure.in
@@ -182,7 +182,13 @@
 	exit(1);
 }, [AC_MSG_RESULT(yes)
     AC_DEFINE(NODLOPEN)
-    HAVEMETHOD=yes], AC_MSG_RESULT(no), AC_MSG_RESULT(no))
+    HAVEMETHOD=yes], AC_MSG_RESULT(no),
+dnl Cross-compiling (OHOS): cannot run test programs (E064 pattern).
+dnl Assume musl, where dlopen("libc.so") returns the already-loaded
+dnl libc handle, so trickle-overload resolves libc symbols on it.
+[AC_MSG_RESULT(cross-compiling: assuming dlopen("libc.so") works)
+    AC_DEFINE_UNQUOTED(DLOPENLIBC, "libc.so")
+    HAVEMETHOD=yes])
 
 if test "$HAVEMETHOD" = "no"; then
     dnl ugly, ugly hack		     
